"""Approximate a lowercase-to-capital-fragment response.

A single capital following a lowercase-ending token gets a negative value.
The response is strongest without a separating space, and after a short
alphabetic fragment. Letter groups calibrate the gain, not the detection.
Spaces, punctuation and the previous fragment's capitalization adjust it.
Bare two- or three-letter uppercase fragments follow a weaker version of
this rule. Bare two-letter titlecase fragments get a small positive value
when not following lowercase. Other tokens are zero; single capitals have
small digit, punctuation and document-start baselines. The previous token
is used only within the current document. No word/token-ID table is used.
