"""A spelling-based sibilant continuation detector.

Short s/z/sh-like fragments tend positive after vowel endings and negative
after consonant endings (especially k/g). Longer words, uppercase words and leading
spaces weaken the response. This approximation covers Latin, Cyrillic, Greek,
and Japanese sibilants; it does not attempt a full pronunciation dictionary.
The gains below summarize training measurements of these recognizable classes.
